# Cloudflare Pages _redirects — gstcalculator.me
# Enforces trailing slash on all URLs

# Blog posts
/blog/:slug  /blog/:slug/  301

# Top-level pages
/blog     /blog/     301
/privacy  /privacy/  301
/about    /about/    301
/contact  /contact/  301

# No wildcard fallback needed here: dist/404.html (built by
# scripts/prerender-routes.mjs) is a real static file at the site root, and
# Cloudflare Pages automatically serves it with a 404 status for any request
# that matches no asset and no rule above. (An earlier `/* /index.html 404`
# rule here looked right but returned an empty body in production — asking
# Cloudflare to rewrite to "/index.html" collides with its own automatic
# index.html-to-"/" redirect. Serving a real, differently-named file avoids
# that entirely and is also Cloudflare's documented convention.)
